WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.130
- We used to terrorize people at school

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.880
and there was one time we
beat up this girl really bad.

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:32.380
It was just a cry for attention, you know?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.607
With my mom.

00:00:35.558 --> 00:00:37.474
(soft music)

00:00:37.474 --> 00:00:38.420
(lighter clicking)

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.240
I was 13 years old and
when I initially started

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.230
hanging out with my gang member friends,

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.730
you wanna say my homies,
you don't think that

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.070
they're bad people, you
think they're (bleep) cool

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.230
because they were, you know?

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.420
We were the people getting in trouble

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.313
and it was fun, you know?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.783
I had a lot of fun back then, but like,

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.663
do I regret some of the things
I did with people, yeah.

00:01:01.654 --> 00:01:04.071
(soft music)

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.563
My mom worked a lot when we were little,

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.113
and she left me home with my brothers.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.783
Even better, I got to have house parties,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.480
come home whenever I wanted.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.930
Mom was never around.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.830
And I'm not saying that
my mom was a bad mom

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.440
'cause my mom was the best mom

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.033
that she could be at the time.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.747
I love my mom to death and
my mom is being the mom

00:01:29.747 --> 00:01:31.933
that I can't be right now.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.750
The first time I lost my kids,

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.380
I was with my youngest son's dad.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:45.320
I was really, really heavily into meth.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.113
Just newly into this relationship and,

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.570
he went to the store
to go steal candy bars,

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.710
two big boxes of candy bars in my vehicle.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.770
They follow him out to the
car, the car doesn't start,

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:59.410
so he leaves my car there
and of course they take

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:02.180
the plate number down and
the cops show up at my house

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.750
a few hours later and long story short,

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.583
there's paraphernalia in the home.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.123
I get arrested for child endangerment.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.653
My children get detained.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.950
I went through hell and high
water to get my kids back.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.990
I ended up getting my kids back

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.503
and I got everything I wanted.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.373
I screwed it up again.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.880
I stayed in that
relationship and I continued

00:02:25.932 --> 00:02:27.693
to get abused.

00:02:33.775 --> 00:02:36.858
And I lost my children because of it.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:40.020
And then at that point in
time, I was literally going

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.760
to jail every month.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.220
Nobody was there, literally,
nobody was there but my mom.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.050
You say these people are your homies

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.470
and they're gonna die for you,

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.300
but they can't even write you a letter

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.693
or club money on your boots.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.823
Like hey how you doin', come
visit you, you know, nothing.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.713
That's what I don't understand.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.650
There wasn't really a process for me.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.023
Like I said, I just kinda faded away.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.033
I just disappeared, you know what I mean?

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.563
And I feel like a lot
of people kinda do that.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.213
But there's a lot of people
that go out the hard way.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.107
I've never seen it happen but
I've heard of it happening.

00:03:29.443 --> 00:03:31.860
(soft music)

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.703
I was in a sober living, I
just got my other kids back,

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:53.773
I needed a job.

00:03:53.773 --> 00:03:55.840
Two, three interviews and think I'm hired

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.090
and then they'll run my
record and it's over.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.130
I won't get a call back.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.563
It's discouraging, you know?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.190
I already knew what it was.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:05.940
I just got out of jail not that long ago.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.847
It makes you feel like a piece of (bleep).

00:04:08.044 --> 00:04:10.300
What can you do, your record's right there

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.080
for everybody to read and you
can't really lie about it.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.720
All you can do is explain yourself,

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.260
like, "Hey, I'm trying
to be a better person,"

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.096
but they don't really wanna hear that,

00:04:18.096 --> 00:04:19.693
all they see is what's black and white.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.573
I had to be an example to my brothers,

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:34.043
and I ended up being the
example of what not to be.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.420
I was the only one out
of all my mom's kids

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.020
that didn't graduate high school.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.450
I was the only one out
of all my mom's kids

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:42.430
to get arrested and
have a record like I did

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.180
to get all my kids taken away from me,

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.793
to, you know, just end up the way I did,

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.260
and to end up getting involved in gangs

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.373
and constantly be
incarcerated, go to rehab.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.270
It's not nothing I'm proud of,

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.413
but all I can do is just
be a better person today.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.603
Just be somebody that
she would want me to be.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.580
I know for a fact that
people that are trying

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.970
to leave gangs or trying to get clean

00:05:08.816 --> 00:05:11.110
are just looking for that one chance

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.600
to make an honest living
or do something positive

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.750
with their life and
they're not getting it.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.000
All they see is what's on black and white

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.350
and what's on their record.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.290
Oh you have a felony or
you have a misdemeanor.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.600
No, you're just a criminal.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.120
And you go to places like Homeboy

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:29.880
and you're not the worst
thing that you've ever done.

00:05:30.574 --> 00:05:32.883
(mumbles) Gang intervention program.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.240
It's for previously
incarcerated men and women

00:05:35.262 --> 00:05:37.873
that just get out of prison or jail,

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.480
try to help them to see
a different way of life

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.390
and help them be rehabilitated.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:44.453
Homeboy Industries means family to me.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.253
It is family to me.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:48.693
It means a second chance to me.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.270
I've gotten an amazing job
at a money manager firm.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.610
Everybody in that firm
knows everything about me

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:57.693
and still encourages me to win.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.740
It's just an awesome feeling
is just to be accepted

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.850
and in an industry like that, you know,

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:09.241
like corporate America
and people see the taxes

00:06:09.241 --> 00:06:12.333
and they don't even trip on it, you know?

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:15.866
Yeah.

00:06:19.561 --> 00:06:20.394
Mhm.

00:06:21.637 --> 00:06:23.063
And I still do at times.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.460
(soft music)

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.918
If I can go back and tell
myself at my lowest point

00:06:30.918 --> 00:06:33.810
(sighs) something encouraging.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.463
I've had some really, really dark moments.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.210
I remember there were even points to where

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:42.030
I didn't wanna be around
but I was like too scared

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.963
to even kill myself, you know?

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.800
Hold on tight, you know,
and be patient with myself,

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.900
'cause I can be very difficult (chuckles).

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.020
But patience has always helped me through.

00:06:55.328 --> 00:07:00.328
♪ I can't wait to fall asleep ♪

00:07:01.076 --> 00:07:06.076
♪ Eyes are heavy, breath is deep ♪

00:07:07.347 --> 00:07:12.347
♪ All is quiet in the street ♪

00:07:13.731 --> 00:07:18.731
♪ Leave the worries that I keep ♪

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:23.901
♪ I'll be tree man ♪

00:07:24.693 --> 00:07:29.693
♪ I'll be tree man tonight ♪

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.917
♪ I'll be tree man ♪

